WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:04.420
Well,

cue-2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:12.900
good day to you. William Hogarth at your
service, painter and engraver. Some would

cue-3
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.880
say satirist too. Some, if you'll pardon
me for saying so, have said

cue-4
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:25.540
genius, but I know no such thing as
genius. Genius is nothing but

cue-5
00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.580
labor and diligence. And so you find me
here,

cue-6
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:37.320
laboring once more at a new set of
pictures. My subject? Why, one of the

cue-7
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:43.780
most contentious, chaotic, and corrupt
spectacles to be seen in these British

cue-8
00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:50.580
Isles during the reign of our sovereign
George II, an election for Parliament.

cue-9
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.080
Why should I want to capture on canvas
such a farcical phenomenon?

cue-10
00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.940
Well, talk of this year's general election
is still fresh on everyone's

cue-11
00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:09.940
lips. Yea, 1754 will go down as the most
absurd of

cue-12
00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:16.840
political contests. At Oxfordshire, they
say 40,000 pounds was

cue-13
00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.820
spent, and even then, no clear result.

cue-14
00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:28.240
If I can show this preposterousness in
paint, it's sure to sell. My four canvases

cue-15
00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:31.080
first, then the engravings I'll make from
them.

cue-16
00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.619
People like a story, and that's what I'll
give 'em,

cue-17
00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:41.539
the story of an election in four scenes,
from the start of the campaign to the

cue-18
00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:47.840
victory parade. And I'll show it all, a
system built on bribery and

cue-19
00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:54.480
bullying, self-interest and sleaze, but
also the great carnival that our

cue-20
00:01:54.480 --> 00:02:01.020
constitution sets going every time there's
a contest. Few can vote, but

cue-21
00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:07.790
everyone can take part. Come, let me show
you my paintings. Each

cue-22
00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:14.640
has a thousand details, comical, strange,
and scandalous.

cue-23
00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:20.160
I satirize the politics of 18th century
England, but perhaps they're not so

cue-24
00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:26.960
different from your own.
